box: the network's own server of names, before anyone has asked:
box: boot: stzos init -- machine makeen_names (hosted / x86_64 / qemu_pc) -- pid 1
box: boot: console /dev/ttyS0
box: boot: mount proc at /proc -- done
box: boot: mount sysfs at /sys -- done
box: boot: mount devtmpfs at /dev -- done
box: boot: grant network (effectful)
box: boot: network salle -- eth0 up 192.168.10.1/24
box: boot: egress salle -- none: the machine knows no way off its own link
box: boot: names salle -- makeen: this machine is 192.168.10.1/24, 2 declared peers, and no address for anyone else
box: boot: names salle -- imprimante.makeen is 192.168.10.50 for 52:54:00:12:34:60
box: boot: names salle -- caisse.makeen is 192.168.10.40 for 52:54:00:12:34:61
box: boot: judge -- the boot matches its expectation (/etc/expected, 11 lines)
box: boot: every service has ended -- and this machine is still makeen: a server stops when the machine stops, not when the asking does
till: the declared device, which knows nothing and asks:
till: boot: stzos init -- machine caisse_makeen (hosted / x86_64 / qemu_pc) -- pid 1
till: boot: console /dev/ttyS0
till: boot: mount proc at /proc -- done
till: boot: mount sysfs at /sys -- done
till: boot: mount devtmpfs at /dev -- done
till: boot: grant process (effectful)
till: boot: grant network (effectful)
till: boot: network salle -- eth0 up 192.168.10.40/24 (dhcp), dns [192.168.10.1], names on makeen (/etc/resolv.conf)
till: boot: start printer -- pid N -- /stzos ask imprimante.makeen
till: ask imprimante.makeen -- 192.168.10.50 (from 192.168.10.1)
till: boot: printer (pid N) exited 0
till: boot: start short -- pid N -- /stzos ask imprimante
till: ask imprimante -- 192.168.10.50 (from 192.168.10.1)
till: boot: short (pid N) exited 0
till: boot: start box -- pid N -- /stzos ask makeen
till: ask makeen -- 192.168.10.1 (from 192.168.10.1)
till: boot: box (pid N) exited 0
till: boot: start absent -- pid N -- /stzos ask fantome.makeen
till: ask fantome.makeen -- no such name on this network (from 192.168.10.1)
till: boot: absent (pid N) exited 0
till: boot: judge -- the boot matches its expectation (/etc/expected, 16 lines)
till: boot: every service has ended -- init has nothing left to keep alive
till: boot: init halts the machine -- reboot(RESTART)
till: reboot: Restarting system
stranger: the same image, with a hardware address nobody declared:
stranger: boot: stzos init -- machine caisse_makeen (hosted / x86_64 / qemu_pc) -- pid 1
stranger: boot: console /dev/ttyS0
stranger: boot: mount proc at /proc -- done
stranger: boot: mount sysfs at /sys -- done
stranger: boot: mount devtmpfs at /dev -- done
stranger: boot: grant process (effectful)
stranger: boot: grant network (effectful)
stranger: boot: network salle -- eth0 dhcp: no lease after 3 tries (no server answered on this network)
stranger: boot: start printer -- pid N -- /stzos ask imprimante.makeen
stranger: ask imprimante.makeen -- no resolver: this machine was never told where to ask (/etc/resolv.conf)
stranger: boot: printer (pid N) exited 0
stranger: boot: start short -- pid N -- /stzos ask imprimante
stranger: ask imprimante -- no resolver: this machine was never told where to ask (/etc/resolv.conf)
stranger: boot: short (pid N) exited 0
stranger: boot: start box -- pid N -- /stzos ask makeen
stranger: ask makeen -- no resolver: this machine was never told where to ask (/etc/resolv.conf)
stranger: boot: box (pid N) exited 0
stranger: boot: start absent -- pid N -- /stzos ask fantome.makeen
stranger: ask fantome.makeen -- no resolver: this machine was never told where to ask (/etc/resolv.conf)
stranger: boot: absent (pid N) exited 0
stranger: boot: judge -- the boot differs from its expectation (/etc/expected): 1 line(s) expected and not said, 1 said and not expected
stranger: boot: judge -- expected, not said: network salle -- eth0 up *
stranger: boot: judge -- said, not expected: network salle -- eth0 dhcp: no lease after 3 tries (no server answered on this network)
stranger: boot: every service has ended -- init has nothing left to keep alive
stranger: boot: init halts the machine -- reboot(RESTART)
stranger: reboot: Restarting system
